@startuml
title Go Application Architecture - Wake-on-LAN Proxy with Pool Manager

actor User
participant "main.go" as main
participant "Config Loader" as config
database "config.yaml" as yaml
participant "Graceful Shutdown Handler" as shutdown
participant "Proxy Controller (proxy.go)" as proxy
participant "Local Port Listener" as listener
participant "Pool Manager (pool.go)" as pool
database "Packet Buffer" as buffer
participant "Monitor (monitor.go)" as monitor
participant "WoL Handler (wol.go)" as wol
participant "Remote System" as remote

== Initialization Phase ==
main -> config: load configuration
config -> yaml: read config.yaml
yaml --> config: config data
config --> main: configuration loaded

main -> shutdown: setup graceful shutdown handler

main -> proxy: startProxy(port, config)
proxy --> main: proxy started

== Runtime Operations ==
proxy -> listener: start local port listener
activate listener

proxy -> pool: create pool manager
activate pool
pool -> buffer: initialize packet buffer
pool -> wol: register WoL handler callback

proxy -> monitor: start monitoring routine
activate monitor

proxy -> wol: start WoL routine
activate wol

monitor -> remote: periodic ping
activate remote
remote --> monitor: awake/asleep status
deactivate remote
monitor -> pool: update remote status (awake/asleep)

User -> listener: send data to local port
listener -> pool: receive packet
pool -> buffer: store packet in buffer
pool -> wol: notify buffer has pending data

wol -> monitor: check current status
monitor --> wol: asleep

wol -> remote: send WoL magic packet
activate remote

== Status Change Flow ==
monitor -> remote: next periodic ping
remote --> monitor: now awake
deactivate remote
monitor -> pool: status changed to awake

pool -> buffer: begin draining packets
loop For each buffered packet
    buffer --> pool: get next packet
    pool -> remote: forward packet
end

== Concurrent Buffer Management ==
Note over pool: Pool manager concurrently:\n- Receives new packets\n- Monitors remote status\n- Forwards when awake

monitor -> remote: continue periodic pings

== Shutdown Phase ==
User -> main: Ctrl+C (SIGINT)
main -> shutdown: trigger graceful shutdown
shutdown -> proxy: stop all components

proxy -> listener: stop listening
proxy -> pool: stop pool manager
proxy -> monitor: stop monitoring
proxy -> wol: stop WoL routine

pool -> buffer: clear all pending data
deactivate pool
deactivate listener
deactivate monitor
deactivate wol

note over main: Application terminated gracefully

@enduml
